    "status": "present",
    "value": "For every linked-list node, return the first later strictly larger value, or zero when none exists. The approach is: monotone unresolved-value stack filled by the first larger node. Its target cost is O(n) time/O(n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
